    "source_turn_preview_server_only": "Insulation slows the movement of heat through materials. However, installing a thick layer in one wall may accomplish little if heat still escapes through an uninsulated roof. These weaker routes are sometimes called thermal bridges. They occur where building components create easier paths for heat flow, so designers must examine details, not merely the amount of insulation purchased."
